t  the execution signatures though were  really cool i don't really use them too  much anymore but the times that i did  use them  i did enjoy them a lot we also got new  armor this time around which is a huge  plus of course the armor was somewhat  well received but met with some backlash  from the community because the dlc one  characters didn't get any new armor  again  the last time they received armor was  back in season eight but it was more  just variations of current  armor they had didn't have any new  original designs  the other thing people mentioned is that  a lot of the armor wasn't exactly  out there so to speak so lots were just  close copies of other armors the  characters had already had  and not much changed minus a few  characters like jorman gunder for  instance  regardless though i was okay with the  armors a bit of a small change as well  but  of course still nice was that the  minions were also being changed we  haven't had a permanent change to the  minions before and it was really cool to  see them change  i am a big fan of the new models and i  feel like they were of course very  needed for the game  executions were also released with the  new season as always these executions  were great there hasn't been one season  i think where they've sucked maybe one  or two seasons they may have been  somewhat lackluster  or maybe not insanely crazy like other  seasons but even those still had a nice  amount of good executions  these have always been consistently good  so no ill wills here with this one  they're always fantastic there was also  two events this season the honor games  and the prince of persia crossover  blades of persia the honor games was  more of a celebration of the game  and added a lot of new things on the  samurai duel map and i missed this  because it actually made the game kind  of feel alive  not just an area where people were  killing each other but some sport was  involved everyone was cheering laughing  and just overall being excited to  celebrate  you know the game and all the  camaraderie going on this added new  emotes in the forms of musical ones that  sadly i don't see too much of honestly  i saw a lot of them during the event but  after it was over they kind of just went  away and i haven't really seen too many  i'm not sure if this is because people  just didn't buy them or had the steel or  maybe people got bored of it i'm not  really sure  but i think my personal favorite was the  community getting involved in having  artists artwork within the game that  changed per week  the game mode was really nice although  it kind of left a sour taste in people's  mouths  as they changed carousel of fire to  carousel of ragnarok  regardless i always thought of carousel  of death game mode and its variations to  be very mindless fun  so this didn't really stress me out too  much overall it was a really nice event  and still my top three sitting at number  two  just below apollyon's legacy the blades  of persia event was like i stated a  crossover event between prince of persia  and  for honor this added lots of changes to  harbor making a sandy desert outpost as  opposed to a dock like normal harbor  the cosmetic items of this event were  really cool as well and are still things  i used today on one of my characters  there's also the introduction of a new  event battle pass of course since they  added the battle pass per season  it kind of made sense that this is the  road they were going to take ultimately  it does fit for the game as it's way  better than before  now you don't need to grind and hope you  get the correct cosmetic item after the  game you've played it's now listed in  the event battle pass and it's free so  there was no negatives to this besides  maybe finishing too quickly but  other than that i think it was way less  frustrating and honestly way better for  the game in the long run  the game mode though pissed me off and a  lot of other people off as well it was  fun 